     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"To make u6 unreachable, every operator for at least one phase must be blocked. Phase u2 cannot be cut because op3 has no blocking toggle. Every other phase has two operators, and each operator needs at least one toggle, so cutting any phase takes at least 2 toggles. Two is enough: t1 blocks op1 and t3 blocks op2, so u1 can never be reached. Equally, t5+t6 cuts u3, t7+t8 cuts u4, t9+t10 cuts u5, and t11+t12 cuts u6. No single toggle blocks every operator of any phase, so the minimum is 2.\"}"
